WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.220
Henry Cavill is apparently not one to mince
words.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:07.740
In a recent interview with Men's Health, the
actor and erstwhile Superman was asked about

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.560
the three films in which he filled out Kal-El's
famous cape.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.550
In responding, he admitted to feeling exactly
like the rest of us do about Justice League.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:20.150
The DC Movie Universe has been on a roll for
the last couple years or so; 2017's Wonder

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.890
Woman was a critical and box office hit, and
more recently, last year's Aquaman and this

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.140
year's Joker have both cleared the billion
dollar mark at the worldwide box office while

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.620
satisfying the fandom.

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:34.620
Prior to these successes, though, the road
was quite a bit rockier — and that rocky

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.520
stretch included the entirety of Cavill's
tenure as Big Blue — so far, anyway.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.080
2013's Man of Steel led off the franchise,
and while it performed respectably, it divided

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.920
fans — many of whom were unprepared for
writer David S. Goyer and director Zak Snyder's

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.980
exceedingly dark vision of the Last Son of
Krypton's tale.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:59.100
That flick was followed by 2016's Batman V.
Superman: Dawn of Justice, a film which probably

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:03.080
should have broken every box office record
in existence due to its pairing of the two

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.770
comic book icons onscreen for the first time.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:10.790
The flick did clear $870 million globally,
but critics were generally not impressed,

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:15.890
and it divided audiences even more sharply;
industry observers noted that the failure

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.660
of a movie with both Batman and Superman in
its title to make over a billion dollars was

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:21.160
troubling.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.240
2016's Suicide Squad, which endured a mid-production
course correction aimed at injecting a bit

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.640
more levity, continued the trend of earning
respectable box office numbers while getting

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.040
mostly trashed by critics — and then came
2017's Justice League.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.620
Wooo, boy…

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.300
"He's back."

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.940
The team-up film reunited Ben Affleck's Batman
and Gal Gadot's Wonder Woman with Cavill's

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:53.140
Superman, and also introduced Jason Momoa's
Aquaman, Ezra Miller's the Flash, and Ray

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.140
Fisher's Cyborg.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.780
Despite production troubles, it was a film
that should have had DC fans over the moon

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.820
with excitement.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:00.900
It... did not.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:06.320
Justice League struggled to a $677 million
worldwide gross, the worst performance for

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.300
a DC Movie Universe film thus far — and
for the reason why, look no further than Cavill's

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.680
assessment of his three outings as Supes.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.270
On Man of Steel, he said:

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.840
"A great starting point.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.140
If I were to go back, I don't think I'd change
anything."

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.980
On Dawn of Justice, he opined:

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.660
"Very much a Batman movie.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.780
And I think that realm of darkness is great
for a Batman movie."

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.100
Finally, on Justice League, he admitted that,
quote, "It didn't work."

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.290
There's no denying that Justice League indeed
didn't work, although things may have turned

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:37.480
out differently had Snyder not handed over
the reins to Joss Whedon following a family

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:37.980
tragedy.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.480
By all accounts, the film turned in by Whedon
was a very, very different one from that which

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.740
would have been fielded by Snyder — so much
so that in the years since Justice League's

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:51.040
release, fans have been lobbying hard for
studio Warner Bros. to release Snyder's cut

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.100
of the film, which the director has said would
need only a few "CGI tweaks" to complete.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.320
Here's hoping!

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.560
"A man I knew used to say that hope is like
your car keys.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:04.420
Easy to lose, but if you dig around it's usually
close by."

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:08.780
The movie's failure, though, has contributed
to the public perception that Cavill may indeed

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.000
be done playing Superman.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.840
His Dawn of Justice co-star Affleck has hung
up Batman's cape and cowl for good, making

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:19.300
way for a different, younger iteration of
the Caped Crusader to be portrayed by Robert

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:24.190
Pattinson in writer/director Matt Reeves'
forthcoming The Batman; while no comparable

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:28.610
Superman project has yet been announced, it
seems like just a matter of time before Big

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.849
Blue gets the reboot treatment, as well.

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:34.959
The perception that Cavill is through was
further bolstered by his non-cameo at the

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:38.629
end of this year's Shazam!, in which Supes
showed up to have a bite of lunch with the

00:03:38.629 --> 00:03:42.820
titular hero — and was portrayed by a stand-in,
shown only from the neck down.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:46.540
For the record, though, Cavill only failed
to reprise his role because of scheduling

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.650
conflicts with Mission: Impossible - Fallout
— and to hear the star tell it, he may not

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:53.420
be as done with Superman as everyone seems
to think he is.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.420
The actor said:

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.890
"The cape is still in the closet.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:56.890
It's still mine.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:59.840
I'm not just going to sit quietly in the dark
as all this stuff is going on.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.280
I've not given up the role.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.060
There's a lot I have to give for Superman
yet.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.680
A lot of storytelling to do.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:08.900
A lot of real, true depths to the honesty
of the character I want to get into.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.680
I want to reflect the comic books.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:11.680
That's important to me.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.390
There's a lot of justice to be done for Superman."

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:17.740
That is far, far more than Cavill has had
to say on the subject in the last couple of

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.280
years.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.860
If we're being honest, we've always felt like
his version of Supes got the short end of

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:26.080
the stick, and his obvious sense of ownership
over the role has us pretty much convinced

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.640
that he should be given a chance to flesh
out the character in a way that his previous

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.680
appearances didn't quite allow for.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:36.100
So: does Cavill have an actual status for
us on the future of his version of Superman?

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.300
According to Cavill, quote, "The status is:
You'll see."

